###############################################################################
#
# SCHISM coupled ike_shinnecock_atm2sch + one-way NWM river forcing
# (USE_NUOPC_RIVER, Increment 1: constant-stub discharge)
#
# Clone of coastal_ike_shinnecock_atm2sch. Differences:
#   - UFS_CONFIGURE uses the _nwm variant (adds OCN attribute river_stub_q)
#   - river_stub_q is exported (uniform constant discharge [m^3/s])
#
# REQUIRES (input-data side, NOT in this repo — stage before running):
#   1. Build the executable with -DUSE_NUOPC_RIVER=ON (see rt_coastal.conf).
#   2. In the staged SCHISM param.nml set  if_source = 1  (default Shinnecock
#      input ships if_source=0).
#   3. Provide a sparse source_sink.in in the SCHISM run dir listing the source
#      (and sink) global element ids. A template is at
#      tests/parm/coastal_shinnecock_source_sink.in.template — replace the
#      element ids with real Shinnecock land-boundary/river-mouth elements
#      (or generate via SCHISM/src/Utility/Pre-Processing/NWM/NWM_coupling).
#   No vsource.th/msource.th are needed: the cap supplies the (constant) volume
#   source and msource uses the ambient default.
#
# NOTE: no baseline ships yet; run and INSPECT (see NWM_RIVER_INCREMENT1_VALIDATION.md).
###############################################################################

